look at this set of numbers twelve  sixteen twelve six eighteen two and four  let's find out the arithmetic mean of  these numbers first we know that it  equals the sum of values divided by the  number of values the sum of values would  be 12 plus 16 plus 12 plus 6 plus 18  plus 2 plus 4 and there are 1 2 3 4 5 6  &amp; 7 7 values we divide this sum by 7 12  plus 16 is 28 28 plus 12 is 40 40 plus 6  is 46 46 plus 18 is 64 and 64 plus 6 is  70 so the mean would equal 70 divided by  7 that gives us 10 so the mean of these  seven numbers is 10 what we are  basically doing is finding an  approximate central value of a given set  of values so there are a couple of other  ways to find the central value to  understand them we first need to arrange  the values in ascending order from the  least number to the highest number 2 as  we can see is the least number we write  a 2 first the next higher number is 4 we  write a 4 next then 6 it is always a  good idea to mark the numbers you have  written with a pencil if the list is  huge there is a chance that you might  miss out a few numbers so 6 would come  next the next highest number after 6 is  12 and it occurs twice so we write 12  and 12 here then 16 then 18 we write 16  and 18 and that completes our list make  sure you have covered all values  arranging it in an ascending order gives  us something called the median the  median is the middle value of the list  when it's arranged in ascending order  there are seven values we have here and  we can see that 12 is the middle value  so the median of this set of values is  12  the median is just another way to  measure the central tendency so the mean  is the average and the median is the  middle value but only after we have  arranged the terms in ascending order  and the third concept is that of a mode  it is the value that occurs more  frequently in our list we can see that  12 occurs twice and all other numbers  occur just once so the mode of this set  of values is 12 why do we have three  concepts to know the central tendency  isn't one enough what are the  applications of each all these questions  will be answered in the coming videos  you
 

